1
00:00:00,620 --> 00:00:02,430
(Amy:)It's not surprising that
the story has captured

2
00:00:02,430 --> 00:00:04,360
(Amy:)the attention of our
little circle of friends.

3
00:00:04,390 --> 00:00:06,120
(Amy:)Are you familiar
with meme theory?

4
00:00:06,130 --> 00:00:08,730
(Sheldon:)I'm familiar with
everything, but go on.

5
00:00:08,730 --> 00:00:11,030
(Amy:)Meme theory suggests

6
00:00:11,030 --> 00:00:13,630
(Amy:)that items of gossip
are like living things

7
00:00:13,630 --> 00:00:16,430
(Amy:)that seek to reproduce
using humans as their host.

8
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:19,670
(Sheldon:)I'm no stranger to
memetic epidemiology.

9
00:00:19,670 --> 00:00:21,540
(Sheldon:)At Johnson Elementary School,

10
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:26,340
the phrase "Shelly Cooper's
a smelly pooper" spread like wildfire.

11
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:28,980
(Amy:)I should think so.

12
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:30,710
(Amy:)That's gold.

13
00:00:34,050 --> 00:00:38,090
(Sheldon:)Your meme hypothesis
does intrigue me.

14
00:00:38,090 --> 00:00:40,160
(Sheldon:)How might we examine
this more closely?

15
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:44,030
(Amy:)Do you have any ethical qualms
regarding human experimentation?

16
00:00:44,030 --> 00:00:49,000
(Sheldon:)It's one of the few forms of interaction
with people that I don't find repellent.

17
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,470
(Amy:)We need to fabricate a
tantalizing piece of gossip.

18
00:00:52,470 --> 00:00:56,870
(Sheldon:)And a second non-tantalizing
piece to use as a control.

